**StrataScratch 10159 — Ranking Most Active Guests (MS SQL Server)

SELECT
    -- Assign rank based on total messages, highest first
    -- DENSE_RANK ensures no gaps when there are ties
    DENSE_RANK() OVER (ORDER BY SUM(n_messages) DESC) AS ranking,

    -- Show which guest this row is about
    id_guest,

    -- Add up all messages this guest sent across all contacts
    SUM(n_messages) AS sum_n_messages

-- Only one table needed
FROM airbnb_contacts

-- Collapse multiple rows per guest into one row
GROUP BY id_guest

-- Final sort: highest message count at top
ORDER BY sum_n_messages DESC;

**Time Complexity (Simple Terms)

SQL Server has to read every row in airbnb_contacts once → O(N) scan
Then sort to compute DENSE_RANK() → O(N log N)
For interview purposes: just say "linear scan plus a sort — standard for aggregation + window functions"

